# Normalise line endings in the repo, whatever Windows checks out locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never diff or normalise these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.glb binary
*.bin binary
*.ttf binary
*.zip binary

# Git LFS is deliberately NOT used here.
#
# The template shipped with every image under LFS. At this repo's size (~54 MB) plain
# git handles it fine, and LFS would cost more than it gives: the Pages workflow checks
# out with lfs:true on every push, so each deploy would draw ~54 MB against the free
# 1 GB/month LFS bandwidth — roughly 18 deploys before builds start failing with an
# error that looks nothing like "you ran out of quota". Anyone cloning without git-lfs
# installed would also get pointer files instead of images, and a confusing build failure.
#
# Reconsider when a single asset passes ~25 MB (a textured Philippopolis reconstruction
# might) or the repo passes a few hundred MB.
